{
  "thesis": "A tall limestone-and-bronze waterfront salon forms the estate’s civic heart: an elevated, deeply shaded living pavilion with a single calm roofline facing the sea. Lower timber-lined suite bars engage its flanks as quiet inhabited buttresses, while a low arrival porch and a broad seaward terrace make the journey from landward arrival to water deliberately legible.",
  "limitationsDeclared": [
    "The scheme uses the required flat-site representation. The waterfront lies conceptually north of the house; no surveyed shoreline, flood datum, setbacks, terrain, retaining work, marine engineering or infinity edge is represented.",
    "The rectangular pool is an editable basin and water volume only; it does not claim an infinity edge, catchment, pool equipment, safety systems or marine construction.",
    "Suite cells establish six generous private suite allocations and direct gallery access, but bathroom layouts, wardrobes, furniture, kitchen equipment, lighting, planting and interior fit-out remain outside the supported envelope.",
    "Saint Lucia hurricane, wind-driven rain, corrosion, drainage, structural, accessibility and local planning requirements require specialist coordination before construction.",
    "US$25 million is treated solely as the client-stated property-value ambition in explicit USD, not as a construction budget, cost estimate or valuation claim."
  ],
